course: dictionary
lesson: 14642
title: Precedence: what comes first
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Precedence means being more important than something else, so it comes first. Think of a queue: the person at the front has precedence over the people behind. «Safety takes precedence over fun, so we put on our helmets before we ride our bikes.» Safety is more important, so it goes first.
explain: In maths, precedence tells you which part of a sum to work out first. «Multiplication and division take precedence over addition and subtraction.» So in 2 + 3 × 4, you multiply first: 3 × 4 is 12, then add 2 to get 14.
explain: You will see precedence in phrases like «take precedence over», «give precedence to» and «order of precedence». If one thing takes precedence over another, it comes before it. Check by asking: which thing is more important here?
fact: Precedence means being more important than something else, so it comes first.
fact: «Safety takes precedence over fun» means safety is more important, so it comes first.
fact: In maths, multiplication and division take precedence over addition and subtraction.
fact: Some people remember this order with the words BIDMAS, BODMAS or PEMDAS.
fact: Order of precedence means the order in which people or things must go, by rank or importance.
exercise: In the sum 2 + 3 × 4, which part should you work out first? | 2 + 3 | Neither, they are the same | 2 + 4 | *3 × 4
exercise: «Safety takes precedence over fun.» What does takes precedence over mean? | *Is more important than, so it comes first | Is the same as | Is the opposite of | Is less important than, so it comes last
exercise: Which phrase means the order in which people or things must go, by rank or importance? | *Order of precedence | Take precedence over | Multiply and divide | Give a good reason
test: «The teacher gave precedence to the youngest children at the water fountain.» What does gave precedence to mean? | Made them wait at the back | Asked them to leave the room | *Let them go first, as more important | Gave them a drink for free
test: In the sum 10 − 4 × 2, which part must you work out first? | Neither, they are the same | 10 − 4 | *4 × 2 | 10 − 2
exam: In the sum 20 ÷ 4 + 1, which step has precedence? | *20 ÷ 4 | They are equal, so it does not matter | 20 + 1 | 4 + 1
